PR Title: feat: Voice Favorites (Pinning)

The Problem Solved: Users lacked a way to save and quickly access their preferred voices from the extensive VoicePicker list. This feature allows pinning favorite voices to the top for immediate access across sessions.

Visuals: [Screenshot showing the UI with the active Star icon and pinned voice](file:///home/jules/verification/screenshots/after_favoriting.png)

Implementation Journey:
- Verified no existing branch existed for this feature.
- Documented brainstorms (Standard vs Minimalist vs Lateral) and chose the Standard approach (persisted localStorage with sorting).
- Added state (`favorites`) and local storage hydration.
- Updated `filteredVoices` logic to sort pinned voices to the top.
- Integrated `Star` icon into the UI with active/inactive styling.
- Captured visual proof using Playwright.
- Passed all linter and build steps (surgically targeting only introduced errors).

Tradeoffs & Assumptions:
- Assumption: I assumed `localStorage` was the best place for this data since there is no user backend DB available.
- Tradeoff: Standard Approach vs Minimalist Approach. I chose the standard approach of persisting the data because temporary session pinning offers less value to someone generating many audiobooks over time.
- I assumed the `react-hooks/set-state-in-effect` rule should be bypassed via inline comment for the initial `localStorage` hydration to avoid SSR hydration mismatch bugs, which is standard Next.js practice.

Testing Instructions:
1. Run `npm run dev` in `web-ui`.
2. Open `http://localhost:3000`.
3. In the Configuration panel, click the Star icon next to any voice (e.g., "Sky").
4. Verify the Star turns yellow and the voice jumps to the top of the list.
5. Refresh the page to verify the preference is saved.

Action Item: `git push -u origin feature/voice-favorites` and `gh pr create --title "feat: Voice Favorites (Pinning)" --body-file pr_manifest.log`
